Glad it’s useful. I’m in **ask mode**, so I can’t edit the file — here’s a concrete way to do it (or switch to agent mode and I can apply it).

### Intent
Keep the title + path/meta line always visible. Hide focus slider, legend, and expand buttons until the pointer is over the header.

### Approach
Wrap everything **below** the path line in a collapsible block, and expand it on `header:hover` (and `:focus-within` for keyboard).

**1. HTML** (in `render_html`) — wrap the control block:

```html
<header>
  <h1>…</h1>
  <div class="meta" id="meta"></div>
  <div class="header-extras">
    <div id="hl-control">…</div>
    <div class="legend">…</div>
    <div id="toolbar">…</div>
  </div>
</header>
```

**2. CSS**

```css
header {
  /* keep sticky; allow hover target even when collapsed */
  transition: padding 0.25s ease;
}
.header-extras {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-rows: 0fr;
  opacity: 0;
  transition: grid-template-rows 0.35s ease, opacity 0.25s ease;
  /* optional: don't steal clicks when collapsed */
  pointer-events: none;
}
.header-extras-inner {
  min-height: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
}
header:hover .header-extras,
header:focus-within .header-extras {
  grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  opacity: 1;
  pointer-events: auto;
}
```

If you wrap children without an inner div, put `min-height: 0; overflow: hidden` on a single child wrapper inside `.header-extras` (same pattern as the folder expand animation).

**3. Optional polish**
- Slightly reduce header padding when collapsed so the tree gains vertical space.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` → skip the transition.
- Touch devices: hover is flaky; either leave a small “controls” chevron to toggle, or keep expanded on coarse pointers:

```css
@media (hover: none) {
  .header-extras {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
    opacity: 1;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }
}
```

That matches your red bracket: path stays; focus slider + legend + buttons only when the mouse is in the header.

